# Beyond the Stars showcase world (automation): a tour of the save as downloaded, filmed in the full pack.
# Nothing is built or fed by this script: every machine is the save's own.

name kerr 194,39,31
name eye1 321,8,25
name eye2 454,8,25
name eye3 587,8,25
name eye4 720,8,53
name eye5 869,8,53
name eye6 1047,8,59
name eye7 1248,8,72
name eye8 1468,8,96
name eye9 2000,8,-90
name eye10 2300,8,-90
name q7 1248,80,222
name q8 1468,80,275
name q9 2000,80,-420
name q10 2300,80,-420
name qhom 1820,80,80
name qcon 2502,80,25
name qlat 3471,100,42
name hom 2047,41,56
name dif 2199,12,160
name ref 2319,10,160
points kerr
points eye1
points eye2
points eye3
points eye4
points eye5
points eye6
points eye7
points eye8
points eye9
points eye10
points q7
points q8
points q9
points q10
points qhom
points qcon
points qlat
points hom
points dif
points ref
time noon

scene title
  card 5 Beyond the Stars | The showcase world: automation | Every top-tier machine of the Singularity Ladder and the Eye of Harmony at all ten tiers, | running on their own: no player, no hand on anything

scene avenue
  caption The avenue runs east from the spawn. Every exhibit stands beside it, and its chunks stay loaded, so it keeps running while you are elsewhere.
  dolly -30,60,-60 420,95,-60 look 600,20,120 seconds 9 ease inout

scene kerr
  caption The Kerr Ergosphere Engine, tier 2, with its Extractor and Compressor Modules. The hole sits at its 512 solar-mass setpoint on an endless bus of bolts.
  orbit kerr.c radius 95 height 30 from -50 to 30 seconds 9

scene eye1
  caption The Eye of Harmony, tier 1: Sol. A star held in a magnetic field, kept stable only by the valves around its band.
  readout eye1 match ^(Star|Field|Pressure|Stability|Integrity)
  orbit eye1.c radius 100 height 32 from -40 to 20 seconds 8

scene valves
  caption Each valve is a GT debug tank (the endless supply) with a Fluid Regulator cover, switched by a Machine Controller cover from the Directive Hatch above it: the star asks, the valve opens.
  goto 548.5,52.5,35.5 look 560.5,47.5,44.5
  label eye3.dir.eye_trims | Directive Hatch (Trims)
  hold 7
  caption On the magnetar (tier 6) the Status hatch's event bit opens the Antipolarization Agent valve when a flare is due.
  label clear
  goto 995.5,53.5,110.5 look 1011.5,48.5,106.5
  label eye6.dir.eye_status | Directive Hatch (Status)
  hold 6

scene eyes2to6
  caption Tier 2, Sirius A, adds the beam band...
  orbit eye2.c radius 85 height 28 from -35 to 15 seconds 5
  caption ...tier 3, Arcturus, the jet crescent...
  orbit eye3.c radius 90 height 30 from -35 to 15 seconds 5
  caption ...tier 4, the neutron star, the spiral arms...
  orbit eye4.c radius 100 height 34 from -35 to 15 seconds 5
  caption ...tier 5, Sirius B, cooling white dwarfs in batches...
  orbit eye5.c radius 105 height 36 from -35 to 15 seconds 5
  caption ...and tier 6, the magnetar. Its flares are answered by an Agent valve on the Status hatch's event bit.
  orbit eye6.c radius 125 height 42 from -35 to 20 seconds 6

scene eye7
  caption Tier 7, Triangulum: a galaxy, fed by a real Quasar Engine. The quasar's jet runs down a wormhole Conduit into the Eye.
  orbit eye7.c radius 175 height 50 from -45 to 10 seconds 8
  caption The quasar behind it: a hole of its own, a burning disc and two jets. A Wormhole Mouth under it takes the jet away.
  orbit q7.c radius 90 height 20 from -20 to 40 seconds 7

scene eye8
  caption Tier 8, the Milky Way: four arms and a bar, satellites crossing the disc. If it is lost, it climbs back by itself through the Galactic Merger.
  dolly eye8.c+0,1,-150 eye8.c+0,1,-110 look eye8.c seconds 6 ease inout
  orbit eye8.c radius 190 height 50 from 0 to 45 seconds 7

scene eye9-10
  caption Tiers 9 and 10 on the far side of the avenue, each on its own quasar. Stellar Field Sensor Hatches steer the Conduit Junctions over GT advanced wireless redstone.
  orbit eye9.c radius 165 height 50 from 155 to 205 seconds 8
  caption Tier 10, the top of the Eye.
  orbit eye10.c radius 170 height 50 from 155 to 205 seconds 8

scene homogeny
  caption The Homogeny, tier 3, on a quasar of its own beside it: GRB Receptor Ports take the stream that powers it.
  orbit hom.c radius 110 height 40 from -40 to 20 seconds 8

scene reality
  caption Reality Diffraction and Reality Refab, the ladder's last line, side by side.
  orbit dif.c radius 110 height 40 from -40 to 0 seconds 6
  orbit ref.c radius 110 height 40 from 0 to 40 seconds 6

scene conduit
  caption A Quasar Engine and the Einstein-Rosen Conduit: the stream comes out of a paired mouth, a Mirror turns it into a Junction, and Burst Thermaliser Crowns turn it into EU.
  orbit qcon.c radius 110 height 10 from -50 to 10 seconds 7
  dolly qcon.c+20,-20,-90 qcon.c+260,-20,-90 look qcon.c+300,-40,40 seconds 7 ease inout

scene lattice
  caption The Supermassive Lattice, level 4, round a quasar with Mk IV crowns: the biggest hole in the world, growing towards 4.19 million solar masses.
  orbit qlat.c radius 175 height -5 from -40 to 40 seconds 10

scene gui-eye
  caption The Eye's own screen (tier 1, Sol): the star's zone, the pressure P against its band, stability, integrity, the lock and the production cycle.
  goto eye1+0,2,-3.5 look eye1
  gui eye1
  hold 5
  close

scene gui-quasar
  caption A quasar's screen: the hole's mass and spin, the disc's energy and flux.
  goto qlat+0,0.2,-3.5 look qlat
  gui qlat
  hold 5
  close

scene end
  card 5 Beyond the Stars 0.26.0 | Download this world from the 0.26.0 release on GitHub | Break what you like: a fresh copy is one download away
